. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         *1*Generate DEPENDENT VARIABLE support_gender_equality_attitudes call
> ed support_h4
.         
.         *Recode nonresponse values (–1 through –8) to missing
.         mvdecode plh0298_v2 plh0302_v2 plh0308_v2, mv(-1/-8=.)
  plh0298_v2: 490237 missing values generated
  plh0302_v2: 490218 missing values generated
  plh0308_v2: 490191 missing values generated

.         *Reverse‐code the "traditional norms" items so higher = more egalitar
> ian
.     gen r_plh0298 = 8 - plh0298_v2
(638,870 missing values generated)

.     gen r_plh0302 = 8 - plh0302_v2
(638,851 missing values generated)

.         *Compute unweighted additive index (range 3–21)
.     egen support_idx = rowtotal(r_plh0298 r_plh0302 plh0308_v2)

.     *Rescale to [0,1]: (support_idx − 3) / 18
.     gen support_h4 = (support_idx - 3) / 18

.         
. 
.     *2*Generate INDEPENDENT VARIABLE firstborn_child_female called 'daughter_
> h1'
.    
.    *Code firstborn_child_female as 1 if firstborn is female (kidsex[01]=2), 0
>  if male (kidsex[01]=1)
.     gen firstborn_child_female = .
(663,123 missing values generated)

.     replace firstborn_child_female = 1 if kidsex01 == 2
(216,749 real changes made)

.     replace firstborn_child_female = 0 if kidsex01 == 1
(229,481 real changes made)

.         
.         *3* Compute the age group of the firstborn child in 2018
.           * (survey year – birth year of first child)
.     gen firstborn_age_2018 = 2018 - kidgeb01    // kidgeb01 = birth year of f
> irst child 

. 
.       *Categorize into three mutually exclusive age groups:
.        *    0 = 0–5 years; 1 = 6–10 years; 2 = 11–18 years
.     gen firstborn_age_group_2018 = .
(663,123 missing values generated)

.     replace firstborn_age_group_2018 = 0 if inrange(firstborn_age_2018,  0,  
> 5)
(20,397 real changes made)

.     replace firstborn_age_group_2018 = 1 if inrange(firstborn_age_2018,  6, 1
> 0)
(36,034 real changes made)

.     replace firstborn_age_group_2018 = 2 if inrange(firstborn_age_2018, 11, 1
> 8)
(76,065 real changes made)

.         
.         *3*Generate CONTROLS VARIABLES sex, age, and education level
.     *Respondent sex → respondent_male (0 = female, 1 = male)
.     gen respondent_male = .
(663,123 missing values generated)

.     replace respondent_male = 1 if sex == 1       // 
(319,343 real changes made)

.     replace respondent_male = 0 if sex == 2
(343,767 real changes made)

. 
.     *Age in 2018 and its square
.     gen age_2018        = 2018 - gebjahr           // 

.     gen age_square_2018 = age_2018^2

. 
.     *Education level (0=Primary or below; 1=Secondary; 2=Post-secondary; 3=Te
> rtiary)
.     gen education_level = .
(663,123 missing values generated)

.     replace education_level = 0 if inrange(pgisced11, 0, 1)
(23,523 real changes made)

.     replace education_level = 1 if inrange(pgisced11, 2, 3)
(173,250 real changes made)

.     replace education_level = 2 if inrange(pgisced11, 4, 5)
(36,552 real changes made)

.     replace education_level = 3 if inrange(pgisced11, 6, 8)  // 
(73,386 real changes made)

. 
